   $q$A youth rowing program is writing a formal grant application. A draft sentence reads: "We need the money real bad to fix our busted boats." Which revision best fits the formal style?$q$, $q$[{"text":"We urgently need these funds to repair our damaged boats.","is_correct":true},{"text":"We need the money super badly to repair our boats.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-intensifier"},{"text":"We really need the cash to fix up our busted boats.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-word"},{"text":"We urgently need these funds to replace our entire fleet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$We urgently need these funds to repair our damaged boats.$q$, $q$The correct choice keeps the need and the purpose but uses formal words like "urgently," "repair" and "damaged." Replacing the entire fleet is formal, but it asks for something the draft never mentioned.$q$, 'draft', null)
