   $q$Read the sentence: "Tidal energy is more predictable than wind power engineers can calculate the strength of the tides years in advance." Which revision fixes the run-on?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Tidal energy is more predictable than wind power because engineers can calculate the strength of the tides years in advance.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Tidal energy is more predictable than wind power, because, engineers can calculate the strength of the tides years in advance.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-comma-with-conjunction"},{"text":"Tidal energy is more predictable than wind power. Because engineers can calculate the strength of the tides years in advance.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-created"},{"text":"Tidal energy is more predictable than wind power, engineers can calculate the strength of the tides years in advance.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Tidal energy is more predictable than wind power because engineers can calculate the strength of the tides years in advance.$q$, $q$"Because" turns the second clause into a dependent clause that explains the first, producing one complete sentence. Placing a period before "Because" fixes the run-on but leaves the second part as a fragment.$q$, 'draft', null)
