   $q$Which detail from the story, placed in the blank at sentence 10, would best support the claim in sentence 11?$q$, $q$[{"text":"On this second visit, he plays a slow scale after each adjustment, just as Mr. Abara did.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Teodor decides that he will open a tuning shop of his own when spring arrives.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"does-not-show-change"},{"text":"Teodor notices that frost has covered the tall church windows during the cold snap.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"setting-not-evidence"},{"text":"Mr. Abara tells Teodor that he once tuned a piano for a concert hall in a large city.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$On this second visit, he plays a slow scale after each adjustment, just as Mr. Abara did.$q$, $q$Playing a slow scale after each adjustment shows Teodor taking on Mr. Abara's patient method, which directly supports the claim about learning to listen. The plan to open a shop is about his future, not about how he now works.$q$, 'draft', 'ed20a3a4-dd83-52e9-ae1c-07011d2f86b0')
