   $q$Why is the quotation in sentence 7 especially effective evidence for the writer's analysis?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is the longest quotation in the draft, so it gives the reader the most information.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"length-equals-strength"},{"text":"It proves that electronic meters are less accurate than the human ear for tuning pianos.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"It shows that the cold snap made the piano much harder to tune than it was before.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-focus"},{"text":"It mirrors sentence 3, showing Teodor now putting the meter away and playing instead of leaving without a chord.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It mirrors sentence 3, showing Teodor now putting the meter away and playing instead of leaving without a chord.$q$, $q$Sentence 3 shows Teodor leaving "without playing a single chord," and sentence 7 shows him playing until the room agrees, so the two quotations together reveal his change. The story is about Teodor's growth, not about whether meters are accurate in general.$q$, 'draft', 'ed20a3a4-dd83-52e9-ae1c-07011d2f86b0')
