   $q$The data set 12, 14, 15, 15, 16, 18 has a mean of 15. If the 18 is replaced by 60, by how much does the mean increase?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$42$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-divide-by-count"},{"text":"$6$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"divided-by-n-plus-one"},{"text":"$0$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"thought-mean-resists-outliers"},{"text":"$7$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$7$$q$, $q$The sum grows by $60 - 18 = 42$, and the mean is the sum divided by the 6 values, so the mean grows by $\frac{42}{6} = 7$, from $15$ to $22$. The median stays at $15$, which shows the mean is the measure pulled by the outlier. The value $42$ is the change in the sum, not the mean.$q$, 'draft', null)
