   $q$The data set 5, 6, 8, 9, 12, 32 has a mean of 12. If the outlier 32 is removed, by how much does the mean decrease?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$4$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$20$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-outlier-from-mean"},{"text":"$8$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reported-new-mean"},{"text":"$0.5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tracked-median-instead"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$4$$q$, $q$Without 32, the values 5, 6, 8, 9, 12 add to $40$, so the new mean is $\frac{40}{5} = 8$. The mean drops by $12 - 8 = 4$. The median only moves from $8.5$ to $8$, a change of $0.5$, which is why the median is called resistant to outliers.$q$, 'draft', null)
